desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Use Escapexml"
	title_zh: "检测到Use Escapexml",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-use-escapexml"
	risk: "xss"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `use-escapexml` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/java/lang/security/audit/xss/jsp/use-escapexml.yaml).
Original message: Detected an Expression Language segment that does not escape output. This is dangerous because if any data in this expression can be controlled externally, it is a cross-site scripting vulnerability. Instead, use the 'escapeXml' function from the JSTL taglib. See https://www.tutorialspoint.com/jsp/jstl_function_escapexml.htm for more information.

CWE: CWE-116: Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output
References:
- https://www.tutorialspoint.com/jsp/jstl_function_escapexml.htm
- https://stackoverflow.com/a/4948856
- https://stackoverflow.com/a/3180202

False-positive hardening: drop JS template/string uses of ${...} (backtick templates and single-quoted JS strings).
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.jsp": <<<POS
<input value="${param.foo}" />
<div>
${param.foo}
</div>
POS
	"safefile://neg.jsp": <<<NEG
<input type="text" name="foo" value="${fn:escapeXml(param.foo)}" />
<script>
const id = `row-${id}`;
applyPermissionChanges('${id}');
</script>
NEG
)

${*.jsp}.pattern_regex_not(/\$\{(?![^}]*escapeXml)[^}\n]{1,120}\}/, /\$\{[^}\n]+\}`/, /'\$\{[^}\n]+\}'/, /`[^`\n]*\$\{/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Use Escapexml",
	title_zh: "检测到Use Escapexml",
	message: "Use Escapexml",
}
